From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:03:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 117/151] Large files: fast open, background preview, windowed
 rendering

A 5 MB Markdown file froze the editor for minutes when it opened:

- iced's Markdown parser copies the rest of its input after every
  top-level item, so one parse of the whole text grows with the square
  of its length (5 MB: 7.7 s in a test, minutes in the app as every copy
  faulted in fresh pages). Plain Markdown longer than 32 KB now goes to
  it in parts split where a top-level item starts: 0.55 s.
- the preview drew all 145,000 top-level elements every frame. A
  preview of more than 1000 elements now draws only the 300 or fewer
  near the viewport, the others' space estimated and then measured
  (the last one drawn too). Leaves are numbered by element, so a
  selection and Copy span the whole document whatever is drawn.
- the outline drew every heading every frame: 15 ms and more a frame
  with 24,000 headings. An outline of more than 1000 headings now draws
  only the rows near its view, with one fixed row height: under 0.1 ms.
- cosmic-text colours the whole file before the first frame (6 s for
  5 MB of Markdown, 0.3 s as plain text). A file over 1 MB of any kind
  now opens without syntax colours, and one that grows past 1 MB loses
  them before it is reloaded.
- a reload replaced the text in one insert, which cosmic-text does in
  time with the square of its lines (90 s for 1.3 MB). It now inserts
  256 lines at a time, still one undo step.

A Markdown file over 1 MB opens in Source with a notice and a Show
preview button; any other file over 1 MB gets a notice that it opened
without colours. Text over 256 KB is parsed on another thread, with a
placeholder until the preview is ready; the text is not copied again
while that parse runs. Normal files behave as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

